{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"lower_band_projection|DERIVATION_TYPES|DerivationType\\\" packages/lhc/src packages/lhc/test docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-tech-arch.md docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in -g '\"'!docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/artifacts/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/team-impl-log.md:30:- glm-4.7 prior pass had left codebase non-compiling (stale imports, dangling DerivationType, unfinished rename, dropped composeTurnRendering, wrong ThreadDbOpener type, broken resolveInferenceProvider). Opus fixed all.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/team-impl-log.md:31:- Added MIGRATION_V9 (deletes stale `lower_band_projection` work items, logs warning).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/team-impl-log.md:129:- `lower_band_projection` → `smooth_turn_compression` (deterministic → inference per-turn)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/test-plan.md:25:| TC-0.3a | `assignment-config.test.ts` | asserts `DERIVATION_TYPES` is not exported and `DerivationType` is not a named type | compile-time / type-level check |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/test-plan.md:27:| TC-0.4a | `restructure-boundaries.test.ts` | asserts schema DDL uses `smooth_turn_compression`; asserts no code references `lower_band_projection` as a derivation type | grep across src |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/test-plan.md:104:| Old work-queue items with `lower_band_projection` kind crash on first open after rename | `restructure-boundaries.test.ts` | open a thread DB seeded with a queued `lower_band_projection` work item → first-open migration deletes the row and logs a warning; no crash | No TC covers the rename's interaction with the work queue. Without this, a dogfooded thread could crash on next open. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/test-plan.md:218:8. [ ] Verify no `lower_band_projection` references remain in source or schema\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:22:| `lower_band_projection` → `smooth_turn_compression` | deterministic composition | per-turn inference compression of smooth turn text |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:26:The `lower_band_projection` derivation kind is renamed to `smooth_turn_compression` to reflect its new role: compressed turn material produced by inference, not a composed lower-band view.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:44:After this epic, every inference derivation has a tuned prompt; deterministic derivations have settled production behavior. Three derivation types change their production method. `smooth_turn_compression` replaces `lower_band_projection` as per-turn inference compression: when a turn closes, LHC compresses its smooth turn text through a small model call, producing compact prose that preserves the exchange's substance. `chunk_summary_detailed` becomes deterministic: it concatenates the compressed-turn material from its member turns with no model call. `chunk_summary_brief` still uses inference, but consumes the smaller compressed-turn material instead of raw smooth turns, producing more compact historical memory notes. `smoothed_prompt` gains input-size gating and a suspicious-output guard. `tool_result_summary` gains a classification layer that parses mechanical facts before the model call.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:51:1. [Per-Turn Compression](#flow-1-per-turn-compression) — `smooth_turn_compression` replaces `lower_band_projection` as inference compression of the smooth turn. AC 1.1–1.7\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:66:- `lower_band_projection` renamed to `smooth_turn_compression`; production method changes from deterministic composition to per-turn inference compression of smooth turn text, with a compression prompt and target range\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:72:- Remove the `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed enumeration and the construction validation loop that requires all derivation types to be present in assignments; derivation type becomes a plain string discriminator\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:108:The `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed array and `DerivationType` union are removed. Derivation types become plain string discriminators in code and SQLite. The construction validation loop that required every derivation type to have an assignment entry is removed; assignments are validated per-kind only for kinds that are configured.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:110:`lower_band_projection` is renamed to `smooth_turn_compression` everywhere: code, schema, prompts, tests.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:128:**AC-0.3:** The `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed array and `DerivationType` union type are removed. Derivation types are plain string discriminators. Construction does not require all derivation types to be present in the assignment config.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:132:  - When: a search for `DERIVATION_TYPES` or `DerivationType` is run\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:139:**AC-0.4:** The derivation type `lower_band_projection` is renamed to `smooth_turn_compression` in code, schema, and prompts.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:143:  - When: a search for `lower_band_projection` is run\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:166:`smooth_turn_compression` (renamed from `lower_band_projection`) is produced by inference compression. When a turn closes, LHC first ensures the turn's member message-level derivations are resolved — `smoothed_prompt` for user prompts and `tool_result_summary` for tool results. Any that are not yet `ready` are re-attempted: inference is retried if no live recovery work exists, and if retry fails, the deterministic floor is used (cleaned prompt text for `smoothed_prompt`, truncated output for `tool_result_summary`). Fallback use is logged. This recovery behavior is unchanged from Epic 06; this epic preserves it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:532:| `smooth_turn_compression` | gpt-5.4-mini | none | 35%–65%, aim 50% | tiny-turn threshold | Turns below threshold pass through; replaces `lower_band_projection` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:612:**Boundary / risk notes:** wide mechanical change (import paths, folder structure, schema string rename) but no behavioral change. Removes the `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed array and the construction validation that required all types present; derivation types become plain string discriminators. The `inference/` module is dissolved: types merge into shared-tech vocabulary, adapter moves next to the deterministic provider, safeCall/classify becomes shared-tech infrastructure, prompts stay grouped under shared-tech.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/epic.md:643:**Delivers:** `smooth_turn_compression` (replacing `lower_band_projection`) as per-turn inference compression of smooth turn text, including the rename of the derivation type.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:6:Restructure SDK module boundaries, rename `lower_band_projection` to `smooth_turn_compression`, remove typed derivation enumeration, and install extended assignment defaults.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:40:**AC-0.3:** The `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed array and `DerivationType` union type are removed. Derivation types are plain string discriminators. Construction does not require all derivation types to be present in the assignment config.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:44:  - When: a search for `DERIVATION_TYPES` or `DerivationType` is run\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:51:**AC-0.4:** The derivation type `lower_band_projection` is renamed to `smooth_turn_compression` in code, schema, and prompts.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:55:  - When: a search for `lower_band_projection` is run\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:111:It also owns the rename and config contract that later stories depend on. `lower_band_projection` becomes `smooth_turn_compression`, `DERIVATION_TYPES` and `DerivationType` are removed, construction validation becomes per-key, and defaults/guards are filled at SDK construction.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:122:- Old `lower_band_projection` work-queue rows must be deleted by a thread-file migration, not left to crash a worker.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:153:| TC-0.3a | `assignment-config.test.ts` | Assert `DERIVATION_TYPES` is not exported and `DerivationType` is not a named type. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:210:- `lower_band_projection` rename is complete outside historical documentation.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/stories/00-foundation.md:211:- `DERIVATION_TYPES` runtime array and `DerivationType` union are gone.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:20:| 6 | Epic AC-0.4 | Rename `lower_band_projection` → `smooth_turn_compression` needs migration path for existing thread DBs | Resolved — designed | Migration detail in §Rename Migration |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:26:| 12 | Rev 2 feedback | Rename handled old derivation rows but not old queued/claimed/failed work items with `lower_band_projection` kind | Resolved — designed | Explicit work-item rule in §Rename Migration |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:35:This epic replaces that provisional state with the tested prompts, model assignments, guards, and classifier that came out of the `derivation-testing/` work. The constraint that shaped this design is that the boundary between LHC and the host does not change: the host still provides one model-call function at SDK construction, and LHC still routes per-derivation-type with provider-lane/model strings. What changes is entirely internal to LHC — the prompts, the production methods, the guards, and the module structure. Three derivation types change their production method: `lower_band_projection` becomes `smooth_turn_compression` (per-turn inference compression instead of deterministic composition), `chunk_summary_detailed` becomes deterministic concatenation (it was an inference call), and `chunk_summary_brief` consumes compressed-turn material instead of raw smooth turns. Two derivation types gain guards: `smoothed_prompt` gets an input-size cap and a suspicious-output check, `tool_result_summary` gets a deterministic tool-result classifier before its model call. Each of these changes traces directly to evidence from the testing work — measured compression ratios, observed model breakdown thresholds, and prompt iterations that produced stable outputs.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:37:The module structure also changes because `inference/` was added as a top-level folder without being a domain or a clean cross-cutting concern, and that drift was not corrected before now. The six domain folders move from `src/domains/` to `src/` top level so the top-level surfaces match the onboarding docs exactly. The `inference/`, `providers/`, `shared/`, and `tech-utils/` folders consolidate into one `shared-tech/` folder that is clearly not a domain. The `DERIVATION_TYPES` typed array and `DerivationType` union are removed because the only code that needed the full enumeration was the construction-time validation loop, which is itself being replaced with per-key validation against the prompt registry.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:221:| `thread-view/internal/select.ts` | MODIFIED | band fallback ladder references `smooth_turn_compression` instead of `lower_band_projection` | shared-tech derivation vocabulary | (downstream of AC-0.4 rename) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:227:| `shared-tech/derivation.ts` | MODIFIED | `DERIVATION_TYPES` and `DerivationType` removed; derivation type becomes plain string | none | AC-0.3 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:228:| `shared-tech/storage.ts` | MODIFIED | schema DDL rename `lower_band_projection` → `smooth_turn_compression`; first-open migration deletes old work-queue rows | none | AC-0.4 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:246:│   ├── derivation.ts       ← from shared/derivation.ts (minus DERIVATION_TYPES, DerivationType)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:276:All occurrences of `lower_band_projection` become `smooth_turn_compression`:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:290:**Existing thread DB rows:** Thread SQLite files may contain derivation rows with `derivation_type = 'lower_band_projection'`. These are handled by:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:293:2. Read queries (turn composition, band rendering, chunk member reads, repair reports) query for `'smooth_turn_compression'` only. Old `'lower_band_projection'` rows are invisible to these queries.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:294:3. Repair/rebuild/recovery writes new rows with `'smooth_turn_compression'`. When a turn's compression is re-derived, the new row supersedes the old `'lower_band_projection'` row by version. The old row remains in the table but is no longer read.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:295:4. Inspect/report queries filter on the current set of derivation types; old `'lower_band_projection'` rows are excluded from reports by default.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:297:6. Old work-queue items referencing `lower_band_projection` as the kind are a hard error after rename — there is no handler registered for that kind. To prevent this, Story 0 adds a **thread-file migration step** (not an informal startup sweep) in the storage migration sequence in `shared-tech/storage.ts`, assembled into the thread-file migration history by `threads/internal/create.ts`: the migration deletes any work-queue rows with `kind = 'lower_band_projection'` and logs a warning. It runs once per thread DB, recorded in the migration history so it never re-runs. These items are safe to delete because the derivation they would have produced is superseded by the next turn-close or recovery pass under the new name.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:299:This is safe because existing `lower_band_projection` rows are only consumed by turn composition and band rendering, both of which will re-derive under the new name when their consumer (chunk close, compact) next runs.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:303:The `DERIVATION_TYPES` array and `DerivationType` union type are removed from `shared-tech/derivation.ts`. All code that previously typed against `DerivationType` now uses `string`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:329:| AC-0.3 | `DERIVATION_TYPES` array and `DerivationType` union removed; derivation type is a plain string discriminator; prompt registry holds inference prompts only, deterministic prompt files removed (§Typed Enumeration Removal, §Target Layout) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:330:| AC-0.4 | `lower_band_projection` renamed to `smooth_turn_compression` in code, schema, prompts, tests; old derivation rows and work-queue items handled by explicit rules (§Rename Migration) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:888:**Architecture-Risk Tests:** Old work-queue items with `lower_band_projection` kind must be deleted on first open (not re-queued) — see test-plan.md architecture-risk row. Import-boundary rules must be enforced by the checker, not just documented.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:895:2. Write test asserting `smooth_turn_compression` is a valid derivation type in schema → fails (still `lower_band_projection`)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:903:4. Remove `DERIVATION_TYPES` array and `DerivationType` union; valid-key authority moves to prompt registry + handler registration\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:904:5. Rename `lower_band_projection` → `smooth_turn_compression` in code, schema, prompts, tests (old derivation rows remain unreadable; old work-queue items deleted on first open with warning — see §Rename Migration)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:969:**Scope:** Replace deterministic `lower_band_projection` composition with per-turn inference compression; add tiny-turn passthrough and target validation.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/07-derivation-dial-in/tech-design.md:1144:| Bulk migration of old `lower_band_projection` derivation rows (proactive delete) | AC-0.4 | Harmless to leave; no proactive cleanup | Never, unless space becomes an issue |\npackages/lhc/test/inference-adapter.test.ts:15:  DERIVATION_TYPES,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-adapter.test.ts:22:  type DerivationType,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-adapter.test.ts:48:function adversarialResponses(): Record<DerivationType, string> {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-adapter.test.ts:124:    for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:32:  DERIVATION_TYPES,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:41:  type DerivationType,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:72:  const overrides: Partial<Record<DerivationType, { provider: string; model: string }>> = {};\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:73:  for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:155:      for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:169:            prompt: assignments[form.derivationType as DerivationType].prompt,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts:209:    for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-classification.test.ts:18:  DERIVATION_TYPES,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-classification.test.ts:224:    for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES.filter((k) => k !== \"smoothed_prompt\")) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-routing.test.ts:15:  DERIVATION_TYPES,\npackages/lhc/test/inference-routing.test.ts:41:    for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-routing.test.ts:94:    for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/inference-construction.test.ts:3:// all seven kinds present (parameterized over the exported DERIVATION_TYPES set so\npackages/lhc/test/assignment-config.test.ts:47:  it(\"DERIVATION_TYPES is not exported from the SDK surface\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/assignment-config.test.ts:48:    expect((api as Record<string, unknown>).DERIVATION_TYPES).toBeUndefined();\npackages/lhc/test/assignment-config.test.ts:49:    expect(Object.keys(api)).not.toContain(\"DERIVATION_TYPES\");\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:4:// carrying a stale lower_band_projection work item must not crash a worker on\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:69:  it(\"no source file references lower_band_projection except the v9 migration cleanup\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:71:      .filter((file) => readFileSync(file, \"utf8\").includes(\"lower_band_projection\"))\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:123:describe(\"AC-0.4 architecture-risk: stale lower_band_projection work items are deleted on first open\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:140:        { subjectKind: \"turn\", subjectId: \"t1\", derivationType: \"lower_band_projection\" },\npackages/lhc/test/restructure-boundaries.test.ts:157:        .prepare(`SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM work_item WHERE payload LIKE '%lower_band_projection%'`)\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/work-handlers.ts:18:import type { DerivationType } from \"./model-call.js\";\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/work-handlers.ts:22:  derivationType: DerivationType;\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:19:import type { DerivationType } from \"./model-call.js\";\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:170:        derivationType: row.derivation_type as DerivationType,\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:194:  target: { subjectKind: SubjectKind; subjectId: string; derivationType: DerivationType },\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:236:  derivationType: DerivationType;\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:16:// enumeration (DERIVATION_TYPES / DerivationType) from src — derivation types\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:21:export const DERIVATION_TYPES = [\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:29:export type DerivationType = (typeof DERIVATION_TYPES)[number];\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:38:function fixturePrompt(kind: DerivationType): string {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:54:  overrides: Partial<Record<DerivationType, Partial<ModelAssignment>>> = {},\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:55:): Record<DerivationType, ModelAssignment> {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:56:  const map = {} as Record<DerivationType, ModelAssignment>;\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:57:  for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:70:export function cannedResponses(): Record<DerivationType, string> {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:71:  const map = {} as Record<DerivationType, string>;\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:72:  for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:82:export function recordingCall(responses: Record<DerivationType, string>): {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:87:  const known = new Set<string>(DERIVATION_TYPES);\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts:96:    return Promise.resolve({ ok: true, text: responses[kind as DerivationType] });\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts:8:import { DERIVATION_TYPES, type DerivationType } from \"./model-call.js\";\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts:110:  assignments: Record<DerivationType, ModelAssignment>,\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts:134:  for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts:143:    const matched = DERIVATION_TYPES.filter(\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts:164:  for (const kind of DERIVATION_TYPES) {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts:183:  DERIVATION_TYPES,\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts:184:  type DerivationType,\npackages/lhc/src/shared-tech/storage.ts:187:// rename lower_band_projection → smooth_turn_compression leaves queued work\npackages/lhc/src/shared-tech/storage.ts:198:            'deleted stale lower_band_projection work items after rename to smooth_turn_compression',\npackages/lhc/src/shared-tech/storage.ts:202:     FROM work_item WHERE payload LIKE '%lower_band_projection%' LIMIT 1;`,\npackages/lhc/src/shared-tech/storage.ts:203:  `DELETE FROM work_item WHERE payload LIKE '%lower_band_projection%';`,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
